          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Ceiling paint and wall paint differ in thickness, sheen and durability because ceilings and walls face different problems. Ceiling paint is thicker, flat and low-spatter to hide flaws overhead; wall paint is thinner and more washable to survive hands and cleaning.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Use flat ceiling paint for ordinary white ceilings, a flat or matte wall paint when you want the ceiling tinted, and a mildew-resistant formula in bathrooms. Our <a href="/best-ceiling-paint/">ceiling paint picks</a> cover the best options for each case.
